'' TKO0807: a keyword cannot name a type, a typedef, an enum or a namespace -- fbc's
'' error 14, 17 for an enum. The KEYWORD and OPERATOR classes are refused for all four; an
'' INTRINSIC is refused only as a namespace name. Measured one declaration per file over
'' all 247 keywords in each of the four forms, 988 compiles, and tiko now agrees with fbc
'' on every one (it refused 2 of the 133 'type' cases before). In this file fbc's own
'' recovery merges some of them -- it reports lines 3, 7 and 13, then a cascade -- so the
'' lines below are the one-at-a-time answers. 'type Base' was the case that was found.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/keyword-type-name.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: keyword-type-name.bas(3,1): error TKO0807
'' EXPECT-OUT: 'base' is a keyword and cannot name a type
'' EXPECT-OUT: keyword-type-name.bas(7,1): error TKO0807
'' EXPECT-OUT: keyword-type-name.bas(8,1): error TKO0807
'' EXPECT-OUT: cannot name an enum
'' EXPECT-OUT: keyword-type-name.bas(11,1): error TKO0807
'' EXPECT-OUT: keyword-type-name.bas(13,1): error TKO0807
'' EXPECT-OUT: cannot name a namespace
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 5
